# Docs and ADRs

Keep Diátaxis types apart. How-to pages give steps. Reference pages list the machinery. Explanation pages hold decisions and trade-offs. Do not mix them.

An ADR lives in `docs/explanation/architecture-decision-records/` and has: context, decision, alternatives, trade-off, cost, and failure behavior. One decision per file.

Write Markdown that GitHub renders. Use relative links. Do not document a pipeline resource that is not in the code yet.

Use everyday words. Name a service setting, then say what it does for a reader. A cue is one subtitle.
